# CODEOWNERS — automatic review routing.
#
# Right now every path resolves to one person, which is an honest picture of the
# project's bus factor rather than a filing error. The file exists so that
# delegating an area is a one-line change instead of a restructure: when someone
# earns the Reviewer rung (see GOVERNANCE.md), add them to their area below.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# Note: CODEOWNERS only requests review; it does not enforce it. Required
# approvals are configured in branch protection.

# ── Default owner for everything not matched below ───────────────────────────
*                                       @MSKazemi

# ── Areas open to delegation (the labels match the area/* issue labels) ──────
# area/agents — coordinator, subagents, playbooks
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/agent/          @MSKazemi
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/cortex/         @MSKazemi

# area/detectors — sensorium + detector engine
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/detectors/      @MSKazemi
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/sensorium/      @MSKazemi

# area/memory — episodes, knowledge graph, consolidation
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/memory/         @MSKazemi

# area/kube-q — the kq CLI and the browser demo front-end
/v4/packages/kube-q/                                  @MSKazemi

# area/deploy — Helm charts, Kind, cloud deploy paths
/deploy/                                              @MSKazemi
/v4/deploy/                                           @MSKazemi

# ── Load-bearing safety surfaces — always route to the lead maintainer ───────
# These enforce the human-in-the-loop and RBAC guarantees. A change here is a
# change to the product's core promise, so it is deliberately NOT delegable to
# an area reviewer (kind/safety on the issue tracker).
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/api/v1/auth.py  @MSKazemi
/v4/packages/kubeintellect-server/app/autonomy/       @MSKazemi
